# Gameplay quality standards

- Define the player-facing outcome and acceptance criteria before implementation.
- Preserve deterministic and reproducible behavior where practical; use the project's existing random seed/RNG approach.
- Keep damage, status effects, targeting, cooldowns, and progression rules consistent across player, allies, and enemies.
- Handle edge cases: target destroyed mid-effect, source despawned, overlapping hitboxes, pause/time scale, scene transition, and simultaneous triggers.
- Avoid hidden power creep. Explain how new content interacts with existing upgrades and difficulty curves.
- For each new ability or enemy, specify counterplay, readability, VFX/SFX cues, and tuning parameters.
- Do not balance by intuition alone when telemetry or simulation can be used. State assumptions and propose measurable tests.
